  data:
  - Connnet: 1. According to different production processes, Chinese tea is mainly
      classified into () major categories
    ChooseConnnet:
    - A. Green tea, yellow tea, white tea, oolong tea, black tea, dark tea
    - B. Green tea, yellow tea, white tea, blue tea, purple tea, black tea
    - C. Green tea, yellow tea, blue tea, oolong tea, black tea, purple tea
    - D. Blue tea, purple tea, white tea, green tea, red tea, black tea
    anwerindex: 00000000
  - Connnet: 2. Dahongpao belongs to
    ChooseConnnet:
    - A. Oolong Tea
    - B. Black Tea
    - C. Black Tea
    - D. Green Tea
    anwerindex: 00000000
  - Connnet: 3. The aroma characteristics of white tea are
    ChooseConnnet:
    - A. Frankincense
    - B. Honey Fragrance
    - C. Chestnut Fragrance
    - D. Slightly fragrant
    anwerindex: 03000000
  - Connnet: 4. China's national tea is ()
    ChooseConnnet:
    - A. Biluochun
    - B. Longjing
    - C. Tieguanyin
    - D. Mao Feng
    anwerindex: 00000000
  - Connnet: 5. Black tea belongs to the category of () tea.
    ChooseConnnet:
    - A. Unfermented
    - B. Micro Fermentation
    - C. Semi-fermented
    - D. Full Fermentation
    anwerindex: 03000000
  - Connnet: 6. The steeping time for preparing and mixing black tea is generally
      around () minutes.
    ChooseConnnet:
    - A.15~20
    - B.10~15
    - ' C.5~10'
    - D.3~5
    anwerindex: 03000000
